        "### Procedure\n",
        "\n",
        "A face perception task was undertaken with participants to elicit the N170 component. The incorporated visual stimuli of faces, cars, scrambled faces and scrambled cars were obtained from @Rossion_&_Caharel.2011 and contained 40 exemplar visual stimuli in each category. For each trial, one stimuli from the four aforementioned visual categories was randomly displayed in the centre of a screen for 300ms. The visual angle of every image was 3.32° x 3.78°, while the inter-stimulus-interval was 1100-1300ms and displayed a fixation point. Clothing, hair and the background were all excluded from the face stimuli, while a background was omitted for the car stimuli. The scrambled faces and cars were phase-randomized based on the facial and car visual stimuli. Participants wre provided two button alternatives which were used to indicate whether the participant was observing an object (face or car) or a texture (scrambled face or scrambled car) for each trial. A total of 320 trials were undertaken for each participant, where the 40 visual stimuli from each category were displayed twice, forming a total of 80 trials for each stimulus category. Each stimuli was randomly presented through a shuffled-sequence, however, each exemplar was only presented once during the first half of the experiment and once during the second half of the experiment. The experiment was conducted in segments of 40 trials. \n",
        "\n",
        "### EEG recording\n",
        "\n",
        "EEG recordings were conducted with a BioSemi ActiveTwo recording system with active electrodes and the amplifier built into the hardware (@BioSemi.2001). An elastic cap was utilised, with 30 attached scalp electrodes that were positioned relative to the 10/20 system:\n",
        "FP1, F3, F7, FC3, C3, C5, P3, P7, P9, PO7, PO3, O1, Oz, Pz, CPz, FP2, Fz, F4, F8, FC4, FCz, Cz, C4, C6, P4, P8, P10, PO8, PO4, O2. The common mode sense (CMS) was positioned at PO1, while the driven right leg (DRL) was positioned at PO2. The horizontal electrooculogram (HEOG) was positioned with electrodes laterla to the external canthus of each eye, while the vertical electrooculogram was positioned with an electrode below the right eye. A low pass filter was implemented utilising a fifth order sinc filter and a half power cutoff at 204.8Hz. This frequency was then digitized with 24 bits resolution as 1024Hz.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Analysis parameters\n",
        "\n",
        "The N170 was stimulus-locked to the visual stimuli. The epochs were taken from -200ms to 800ms around stimulus onset. The baseline period was measured from -200ms to 0ms. The electrode site for the N170 was PO8. All data and procedural actions were obtained from the ERP CORE resource (@Kappenman_et_al.2021) under a Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0). \n",
        "\n",
        "#### Preprocessing parameters"
